TASK CHORE54
	TITLE "The cli- packages declare no script running their command, the root scripts being its"
		+ "only entry"
	STATUS implemented
	SPEC "packages/cli-merge/package.json declares no merge or node:merge script"
		IMPL "scripts/check-package-scripts.spec.ts::When a cli- package script runs its own entry"
			+ "point"
		IMPL "package.json::check:package-scripts"
	SPEC "packages/cli-validate/package.json declares no validate or node:validate script"
		IMPL "scripts/check-package-scripts.spec.ts::When a cli- package script runs its own entry"
			+ "point"
		IMPL "package.json::check:package-scripts"
	SPEC "no package.json of the repository runs bun with --cwd"
		IMPL "scripts/check-package-scripts.spec.ts::When a package script runs bun with --cwd"
		IMPL "package.json::check:package-scripts"
	SPEC "the real-process tests of bun merge, bun validate, bun run node:merge and bun run"
		+ "node:validate pass unchanged"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.version.spec.js::the root script of Bun"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.version.spec.js::the root script of Node"
		IMPL "packages/cli-validate/cli/validate-cli.version.spec.js::the root script of Bun"
		IMPL "packages/cli-validate/cli/validate-cli.version.spec.js::the root script of Node"
	DELIVERED_BY 196
	RATIONALE "The package scripts duplicate the root ones and nothing invokes them: no document,"
		+ "workflow or script of the repository names them. The Bun ones reach the root through"
		+ "--cwd ../.., a root-relative path in a package script; the Node ones run from the"
		+ "package directory, so the merge defaults to packages/cli-merge/input where bun merge"
		+ "reads input/. The root scripts already run the entry points directly, bun run --filter"
		+ "being rejected for the prefixes it adds to every line. Exposing the commands through a"
		+ "package bin was examined and set aside: Bun links the bin of a workspace package at the"
		+ "root only when the root depends on it, the entry point carries no shebang, and a bin"
		+ "cannot pass the --import of the Node module hooks"
		REF @DECISION.TheRootCliScriptsRunTheirEntryPointDirectly
		REF @DECISION.NodeCommandsRunSourcesThroughModuleHooks
	SOURCE "Owner's draft of 2026-09-20, commit 4aeee6d pushed without a pull request; refined with"
		+ "the owner on 2026-09-26"

TASK CHORE56
	TITLE "bun run guards runs every repository guard, a failing one not stopping the others"
	STATUS implemented
	SPEC "bun run guards runs every check: script of the root package.json and validate:tables, no"
		+ "list of the guards being written anywhere"
		IMPL "package.json::\"guards\""
	SPEC "each guard stays runnable alone as bun run check:<name>"
		IMPL "package.json::\"check:anchors\": \"bun scripts/check-corpus-anchors.ts\""
	SPEC "a failing guard does not stop the others; the run names every guard that failed and exits"
		+ "non-zero"
		IMPL "package.json::--no-exit-on-error"
	SPEC "no script, workflow, AGENTS.md, file of agents/, page of docs/wiki, README or active"
		+ "DECISION or PROCESS names check:guards any more; the dated usage reports keep it"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::- run: bun run guards"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::- `bun run guards`"
		IMPL "agents/worktree.md::- `bun run guards`"
		IMPL "docs/wiki/development.md::bun run guards"
	SPEC "the decision on the repository guards states that a guard is a check: script of the root"
		+ "package.json, that the script running them all bears a name outside check:, and that a"
		+ "failing guard does not stop the others"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::A failing guard does not stop the"
			+ "others"
	RATIONALE "The guards decision names check:guards as its implementation. check:guards chains"
		+ "fourteen bun run calls with &&, grows by one with each guard and stops at the first"
		+ "failure. Bun 1.4.2 runs the scripts matching a pattern itself: bun run --sequential"
		+ "--no-exit-on-error \"check:*\" validate:tables runs them all, prints Exited with code N"
		+ "for each one that fails and exits non-zero, so no orchestrator file is written. An"
		+ "aggregate named check:guards matches its own pattern and runs itself without end, hence"
		+ "the name guards; renaming the thirteen guards under a guard: prefix was set aside for"
		+ "touching more names, and a TypeScript orchestrator for redoing what Bun does. --parallel"
		+ "is not used: the whole chain takes half a second, and sequential output stays in order"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	SOURCE "Raised in the review of pull request 101; refined with the owner on 2026-09-26"
		PR 101
	DELIVERED_BY 195

TASK CHORE58
	TITLE "investigate running awawa in CI, then deliver in the same pull request the change the"
		+ "user picks from the findings"
	STATUS archived
	ARCHIVED_ON 2026-09-26
	DESC "archived undone: awawa runs on ubuntu-latest but has no public install source, and the"
		+ "owner ruled after reading the investigation to keep it out of CI"
	SPEC "the pull request body reports whether awawa can be installed in a GitHub Actions runner,"
		+ "from which source and at which cost per run"
	SPEC "the pull request body reports, for each place named in the rationale, the lines awawa in"
		+ "CI would remove or the check it would add, and whether that gain is worth the"
		+ "installation"
	SPEC "the change the user picks after reading that report is delivered in the same pull"
		+ "request, and the report leaves the body once the change is in"
	RATIONALE "awawa is today a local x86-64 binary, 2.7.0 in ~/.local/bin, 1.6 MB and dynamically"
		+ "linked, installed from a local archive awawa-2.7.0+gd66a2ad-dirty-linux-x86_64.zip under"
		+ "the MIT licence, whose install.sh copies its bin/ and whose README gives no download"
		+ "URL; the repository names no source to install it from. Three places would change: the"
		+ "corpus parser of scripts/check-corpus-anchors.ts and its spec, which awawa show or"
		+ "status --json would replace, and the whole guard if lint L016 consulted git instead of"
		+ "the disk; a CI run of awawa fmt --check and awawa lint --strict, which no job runs"
		+ "today, so the conformance of the corpus is checked only on the machine of its author;"
		+ "and the SPEC of CHORE63, proven in pull request 129 by a manual probe because no test"
		+ "may run awawa in CI, which a test could then prove. Ruled with the user on 2026-09-23:"
		+ "the findings go to the pull request body, not to a file; the user picks the change after"
		+ "reading them and it lands in the same pull request without a DECISION; the task"
		+ "therefore runs in an interactive session, never as an unattended wave agent"
		REF @TASK.CHORE63
	SOURCE "Review of pull request 101"
		PR 101
	SOURCE "Owner ruling on the investigation report: no awawa in CI, the task abandoned"
		PR 190

TASK REFACTOR59
	TITLE "the repository guards read files, import specifiers and corpus lines through shared"
		+ "modules"
	STATUS todo
	SPEC "the file walk of the shared script port scans the root it receives, never process.cwd():"
		+ "a guard run from another directory reports the same violations as one run from the root"
	SPEC "the reading of import specifiers, static and dynamic, is declared once and used by"
		+ "check:presentation and check:dependencies"
	SPEC "the filter of generated directories is declared once and used by every guard that skips"
		+ "them"
	SPEC "no guard imports from another guard: the reading of corpus lines used by check:anchors"
		+ "and check:audit-ignores lives in a shared module"
	SPEC "the main function of a script returns its exit code and no port carries an exit:"
		+ "runAsEntryPoint alone calls process.exit, and a script test asserts the returned code"
	SPEC "the script port is split by responsibility, files apart from console, and no guard"
		+ "receives a port member it never calls"
	SPEC "a script test reading a file the fake does not hold fails naming that path"
	SPEC "a guard fails when a check-*.ts file of scripts/ imports Glob or readdir"
	SPEC "the helpers the guards share live in scripts/helpers/, one file per responsibility, and"
		+ "neither scripts/specSources.ts nor scripts/scriptIo.ts exists"
	SPEC "the guards decision and the script injection decision name scripts/helpers/ as the place"
		+ "of the shared helpers, their IMPL anchors following them"
	SPEC "on the repository at the base commit, every guard reports the same violations and exits"
		+ "with the same code as before the task"
	AFTER @TASK.TEST123
	RATIONALE "The guards decision requires what guards share to be declared once in a common"
		+ "module. TEST123 delivered part of it in pull request 197: every guard reads its files"
		+ "through the ScriptIo port of scripts/scriptIo.ts, the only module importing Glob, and"
		+ "check-package-dependencies prints through reportViolations. What remains on that head:"
		+ "the port scans process.cwd() instead of a root it receives; the dynamic import specifier"
		+ "pattern is copied in check-presentation-entities and check-package-dependencies; the"
		+ "generated-directory filter is copied in five guards and specSources; check-audit-ignores"
		+ "imports readCorpusLines and removeQuotes from check-corpus-anchors; scripts/helpers/"
		+ "does not exist. Ruled with the owner on 2026-09-26 after the review of 197: exit leaves"
		+ "the port, the main function returning its code and runAsEntryPoint alone exiting,"
		+ "because a fake exit that returns lets the test run past the point the real process"
		+ "stops; the port is split so that a guard using one member (listTrackedFiles for"
		+ "check:anchors, commandLineArguments for validate:tables) does not receive seven; the"
		+ "fake readText fails on a path it does not hold instead of yielding undefined;"
		+ "runAsEntryPoint and its process adapter stay duplicated in"
		+ "packages/core-mapping/scripts/sectionValidatorsFile.ts, a package importing no root"
		+ "script and the helper package being refused. One pull request, in commits the review"
		+ "reads in order: port and exit, the move to scripts/helpers/, the shared readings, the"
		+ "Glob guard; each green on bun test and bun run guards. No helper package is created:"
		+ "every consumer lives in scripts/, which is no package. The name specSources dates from"
		+ "pull request 15, when the module served only the guards reading spec files; it now"
		+ "gathers unrelated helpers, hence one file per responsibility. check:section-validators"
		+ "and validate:tables are package scripts and stay out. Distinct from CHORE56, which"
		+ "changes how the guards are run, not the code they share"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
		REF @DECISION.AScriptTestInjectsItsInputAndOutputAndCoverageIgnoresTheRealAdapter
		REF @TASK.TEST123
		REF @TASK.CHORE56
	SOURCE "Raised in the review of pull request 101; refined with the owner on 2026-09-26"
		PR 101
	SOURCE "Re-refined with the owner on 2026-09-26, after the review of the pull request"
		+ "delivering TEST123"
		PR 197

