TASK CHORE130
	TITLE "a changelog entry names the dependency a feature or a fix came from instead of listing"
		+ "its commit"
	STATUS implemented
	SPEC "a feat, fix or breaking commit that changes no path of the directory of a tool is never"
		+ "listed in the changelog entry of that tool, whatever its subject says"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::should give the line of that dependency"
			+ "instead of its commits"
	SPEC "a feat, fix or breaking commit that changes a path of the directory of a tool is listed"
		+ "in the entry of that tool even when its scope names another tool"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::When a commit scoped to another tool"
			+ "changes the directory of the consumer"
	SPEC "every workspace package other than a cli-* or ui-* one declares in its package.json the"
		+ "changelog line of its updates: Core engine updated for core-mapping, Save file format"
		+ "updated for shared-save-processing, Runtime platform updated for shared-platforms and"
		+ "util-types"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/package.json::Core engine updated"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/package.json::Save file format updated"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/package.json::Runtime platform updated"
		IMPL "packages/util-types/package.json::Runtime platform updated"
	SPEC "an entry whose version received a feat, fix or breaking commit through a dependency"
		+ "reads, after the commits of the tool itself, the line of each dependency that commit"
		+ "changed, a line shared by two dependencies written once"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::should list its own features, then the"
			+ "line of the dependency"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::should write that line once, after the"
			+ "line of the other dependency"
	SPEC "an entry whose version received such commits through dependencies only reads their lines"
		+ "alone, and one holding no feat, fix or breaking commit at all still reads - Maintenance"
		+ "changes only"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::should give the line of that dependency"
			+ "instead of its commits"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::should give the entry a single line saying"
			+ "it holds maintenance changes only"
	SPEC "bun run release refuses a release in which a dependency declaring no changelog line"
		+ "received a feat, fix or breaking commit, naming that package"
		IMPL "scripts/release/release.spec.ts::should refuse the release, naming that dependency"
		IMPL "scripts/release/release.spec.ts::should leave the manifest of the consumer untouched"
	SPEC "docs/wiki/releases.md names the dependency lines beside the maintenance line"
		IMPL "docs/wiki/releases.md::changelogLine"
	DELIVERED_BY 209
	RATIONALE "The release script lists on a tool every user-facing commit that touches a path the"
		+ "tool reaches, and prints the subject of the commit as it stands. A commit that touches"
		+ "only core-mapping therefore reaches cli-merge and cli-validate under a subject that"
		+ "names the UI, which tells their reader nothing. The owner ruled on pull request 199 that"
		+ "a commit is never reworded and none is invented: what a tool receives from a dependency"
		+ "reads as a fixed sentence, as the maintenance line already does, the entry of"
		+ "cli-validate of 0.1.1 reading Core engine updated. Ruled at refinement: the dependency"
		+ "line joins the own commits of a tool rather than only replacing an empty list, so a fix"
		+ "of the engine that changes the output of a CLI is never silent; the paths of a commit"
		+ "decide which tools list it, never its scope, since scopes name corpus areas and guards"
		+ "as often as packages, so 35fbec1 feat(cli-merge), which changes the report of"
		+ "cli-validate, is listed on both; each dependency carries its own line in its manifest so"
		+ "a new package cannot be released without one, rather than a single sentence for every"
		+ "dependency or a map kept in the release script. The second SPEC of"
		+ "@DECISION.AChangelogEntryListsOnlyUserFacingCommits is rewritten in place by the task,"
		+ "carrying these refusals as REJECTED"
		REF @DECISION.AChangelogEntryListsOnlyUserFacingCommits
		REF @DECISION.ConsumerVersionsAreComputedByARepositoryScript
	SOURCE "Owner review of pull request 199, the release of cli-merge, cli-validate and"
		+ "ui-save-manager 0.1.1: the changelog entries listed commits of other tools, and the"
		+ "owner asked for a generic sentence rather than a reworded or invented commit"
		PR 199

