TASK TEST147
	TITLE "Locate the elements of the end-to-end scenarios by test id, not by the HTML structure"
	STATUS implemented
	DESC "ratified by the owner on 2026-09-27; the task writes the decision that justifies the test"
		+ "id and rewrites the decisions it reverses"
	SPEC "a DECISION of the corpus records that a UI test must not break on a change of the DOM"
		+ "structure, and justifies by it locating by a data-testid attribute"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::DECISION"
			+ "AUiTestDoesNotBreakOnAChangeOfTheDomStructure"
	SPEC "the UI scenarios locate the elements they act on and assert by a data-testid attribute,"
		+ "so that a change of the HTML structure alone breaks none of them"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/warnings.e2e.ts::getByTestId('display-warnings-messages')"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/merge.e2e.ts::getByTestId('merge')"
	SPEC "check:locators accepts a test id in scenario files"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::When a scenario designates elements by their"
			+ "test id"
	SPEC "the decisions that the locator guard refuses what the screen does not show and that a UI"
		+ "scenario asserts what the screen shows are rewritten in place wherever they contradict"
		+ "the new decision, which they cite as their reason"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::Refusing a test id and accepting a"
			+ "role, label or text locator"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::What the screen shows is the"
			+ "assertion, not the locator"
	SPEC "the process that a test task changes the UI only for its own sake states that a"
		+ "data-testid attribute is a neutral attribute that does not change the UI, and so is not"
		+ "an interface change it governs"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/processes.awawa::A data-testid attribute is a neutral"
			+ "attribute"
	DELIVERED_BY 207
	RATIONALE "Asked by the owner on a review of the save manager redesign, where a warnings"
		+ "scenario reaches the warning list through the main landmark and its list items, a"
		+ "locator a change of layout breaks. The locator guard refuses a test id because a"
		+ "scenario designates what the screen shows; the owner ruled that a UI test must not break"
		+ "on a change of the DOM structure, and that this ruling, recorded as a decision by the"
		+ "task, justifies the test id and replaces that reason. The scenarios locate by test id"
		+ "every element they act on or assert, so every such element carries one, and a role,"
		+ "label or text locator no longer designates one. The test task process holds: a test id"
		+ "changes nothing the user sees or uses, so adding one is not the interface change the"
		+ "process refuses. That statement goes into the process rather than into the new decision,"
		+ "since nothing in the repository anchors it and the corpus writes a rule with nothing to"
		+ "anchor as a process. Dropping the role locators drops the accessibility checks they"
		+ "carried, the status role of the busy indicator in the loading state scenarios among"
		+ "them; those checks move to the accessibility tests of TEST148, not back into the"
		+ "scenarios"
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
		REF @DECISION.AUiScenarioAssertsWhatTheScreenShows
		REF @PROCESS.ATestTaskChangesTheUiOnlyForItsOwnSake
		REF @TASK.TEST148
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SOURCE "Owner review comment on packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/warnings.e2e.ts line 21: add a"
		+ "draft task on master, the end-to-end tests use data-testid so they no longer depend on"
