TASK TEST148
	TITLE "Test the accessibility of the save manager in a category of its own, apart from the"
		+ "scenarios"
	STATUS implemented
	DESC "ratified by the owner on 2026-09-28; the task writes the decision that separates"
		+ "accessibility tests from UI scenarios"
	SPEC "a DECISION of the corpus records that the UI tests are split in two categories: the"
		+ "scenarios, which exercise a user flow, and the accessibility tests, which test only"
		+ "accessibility"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::DECISION"
			+ "AUiTestIsEitherAScenarioOrAnAccessibilityTest"
	SPEC "the accessibility tests form a category of their own, apart from the scenario files, and"
		+ "assert nothing but accessibility"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/accessibility/overview.e2e.ts::Overview page"
			+ "accessibility"
	SPEC "no UI scenario asserts an accessibility property for its own sake"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/merge.e2e.ts::should show the tooltip that describes it'"
	SPEC "the accessibility checks the scenarios lose by locating by test id, the status role of"
		+ "the busy indicator in the loading state scenarios among them, are covered by the"
		+ "accessibility tests"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/accessibility/overview.e2e.ts::toHaveRole('status')"
	SPEC "the accessibility tests live in packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/accessibility.e2e.ts, a"
		+ "Playwright spec run by bun run test:ui on the three engines of the scenarios"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/playwright.config.ts::testMatch: '**/*.e2e.ts'"
	SPEC "an accessibility test reaches an element by its test id and asserts its role, its"
		+ "accessible name or its label with toHaveRole, toHaveAccessibleName or"
		+ "toHaveAccessibleDescription, so that check:locators accepts the file unchanged"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/accessibility/merge.e2e.ts::toHaveAccessibleDescription("
	SPEC "an axe audit of the page, before a save is loaded, once a save is visualized and once a"
		+ "merge result is shown, reports no WCAG 2 A or AA violation"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/helpers/createAWcag2Audit.ts::withTags(wcag2LevelAAndAaTags)"
	SPEC "@axe-core/playwright is a development dependency of ui-save-manager"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/package.json::\"@axe-core/playwright\""
	RATIONALE "Ruled by the owner while ratifying TEST147: once the scenarios locate by test id,"
		+ "their role, label and text locators no longer check the roles and accessible names they"
		+ "used to, and accessibility is to be tested on purpose in a category that tests nothing"
		+ "else rather than as a side effect of a locator. Ruled at the refinement of 2026-09-28:"
		+ "the category is written as hand-written Playwright assertions of the intended roles and"
		+ "names plus an axe audit, because an audit reports what is broken, a field without a"
		+ "label, but not a missing intended role, a busy indicator without the status role being"
		+ "no violation; it holds one file, accessibility.e2e.ts, while master has one page, split"
		+ "into e2e/accessibility/ with one file per page once the redesign brings its pages; it is"
		+ "delivered on master outside any wave, since TEST147 left the gap on master, and the"
		+ "redesign waves carry the tests over to their pages; it runs in the workflow and on the"
		+ "engines of the scenarios, each engine building its own accessibility tree. The checks"
		+ "TEST147 removed: the status role of the two busy indicators; the heading role and level"
		+ "of the section titles; the accessible names of the Visualize and Merge buttons and of"
		+ "the swap button, named by its tooltip; the labels of the three file inputs; the group"
		+ "role and name of the drop areas; the tooltip role; the link role of the download; the"
		+ "contentinfo role of the footer; the list item role of the validation messages"
		REF @TASK.TEST147
		REF @DECISION.AnIconOnlyButtonIsNamedByItsTooltip
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
		REF @DECISION.UiScenariosArePlaywrightSpecsOnThreeEngines
		REF @PROCESS.ATestTaskChangesTheUiOnlyForItsOwnSake
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SOURCE "Owner ruling of 2026-09-27: the UI tests that check accessibility are separated into a"
		+ "category of their own that tests only accessibility, the UI tests focus on the"
		+ "scenarios, as a second task and a second decision drafted on the same pull request"
		PR 206
	SOURCE "Owner ruling at the refinement of 2026-09-28: Playwright assertions plus an axe audit,"
		+ "one accessibility.e2e.ts split by page later, delivered on master outside any wave"
